<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cedula of Population</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1783</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Cédula de Población, Real Cédula de Población</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cédula de Población was a royal decree issued by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iii-of-spain">Charles III of Spain</a> in 1783 to encourage the settlement of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trinidad">Trinidad</a>. It offered free land, tax exemptions and other privileges to Catholic immigrants from friendly nations, with additional land for each enslaved person they brought. It drew many French planters and free people of colour from the French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>, giving the island a strong French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/criollo-people">Creole</a> character.</p></div>
